o complete chow is low (would need T4 and T6, both scarce).  \n- T1\u2013T3 kept can form chow if I draw T4 (2 left).  \n- T7 pair kept gives me a ready pair for final hand.  \n- W4 and W5 are less connected but could pair or chow with W3/W6 draws.  \n- Discarding T5 preserves more flexibility: keeps T1\u2013T3 for low chow, keeps T7 pair, and doesn\u2019t break potential W chow.  \n\nBest discard is **T5** to reduce isolated middle tiles and keep sequence potential.  \n\n**Answer: Play T5**"}
